F2 evidence — hmi/config.yaml's DESIGNED connect failure, made legible (m5-29b)
===============================================================================

Produced on the Windows showcase machine, 2026-08-05, by running hmi_server.py
against `plc/forklift/double/server.py` (port 4850) — a server that carries the
opcua-nodes.md §10 set and NO §12 node, which is exactly the shape of the
commissioned CPU today. The configuration used was hmi/config-v2a-double.yaml
with the endpoint repointed at that double and the HTTP port moved off 8094;
the repointed copy was a scratch file and is deliberately not committed.

No PLC was contacted. Nothing here is evidence about the TIA build.

BEFORE (m5-29 finding 2, quoting the review): the operator saw
    connect failed: BadNoMatch ... (retry in 1.0 s)
naming no node and no browse path, forever.

